    {
      "title": "Bumble has a Billion Dollar Tax Shield / $440M Market cap / $200M FCF",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "March 4, 2026",
      "summary": "This due diligence memo highlights Bumble's balance sheet tax arbitrage following its Q4 repurchase of the Tax Receivable Agreement (TRA) liability for $186M in cash, unlocking $419M\u2013$692M in wholly owned deferred tax assets. Discounted at 10% over 11 years, the conservative present value of this tax shield ($247M\u2013$409M) virtually covers the company's entire $440M market cap. This structure permits BMBL to convert its ~$200M in annual operating cash flow into tax-free earnings to quickly eliminate net debt and retire equity.",
